       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. 6,000 mg/day of acetaminophen is well above the maximum daily dose and could cause serious liver injury. Normal liver function and a weight of 70 kg don't make that dose safe. I can't think of a routine indication that justifies it.\n\nIf you have a specific reason for the higher dose, such as a toxicology recommendation, please discuss it with your attending and pharmacy. They can enter or verify the order through the proper override process.\n\nI can enter any of these right away:\n- 1000 mg PO three times daily (3,000 mg/day)\n- 1000 mg PO four times daily (4,000 mg/day)\n- 650 mg PO every 6 hours (2,600 mg/day)\n\nIf the pain isn't controlled at those doses, I can help you think through adding another analgesic."
